menu "UART_ECHO_Polling"

config UART_ECHO_BAUD_RATE
    int "UART0 baud rate"
    range 1200 3000000
    default 19200
    help
        Baud is used after the bootROM has been inserted into the driver. This Baud does not change the
        configuration baud of the bootROM on the FPGA.

config UART_ECHO_FIXED_CLOCK_HZ
    int "Fixed FPGA clock (Hz; 0 uses normal SDK clock setup)"
    range 0 1000000000
    default 10000000
    help
        External clock specified by FPGA; defaults to 10 MHz as Test_VP. values other than 0 apply to both
        SystemInit, driver and onboard. select 0 to use the SDK's normal clock itself. must match
        the actual clock frequency supplied by the board.

config UART_ECHO_RX_TIMEOUT_POLLS
    int "RX timeout (poll iterations, not milliseconds)"
    range 1 100000000
    default 10000
    help
        Polling budget for receiving one byte. Exhausting the budget without data is normal while idle
        state; cancer user continues to receive.

config UART_ECHO_TX_TIMEOUT_POLLS
    int "TX timeout (poll iterations, not milliseconds)"
    range 1 100000000
    default 1000000
    help
        Budget poll for a single byte transfer. when timeout, write receive state and return to receive; do
        not automatically reguise bytes because no may have been written in the UART register before
        the driver gave an error.

endmenu
